General requirements. Recipients are encouraged to discuss the following topics, as it relates directly to your project, with reporters, journalists, or trade publications:

• The purpose, goals, and scope of your project;

• The scientific or technical approach your team is using;

• Progress updates, milestones reached, or innovations developed;

• Expected or observed project outcomes;

• Collaborators, partners, or institutions involved in your project;

• Your organization’s role including project execution;

• Technical expertise and contributions of the team;

• How the work supports the objectives outlined in the USDA NWS GC funding opportunity announcement; and,

• Publicly available information contained in USDA announcements or fact sheets.

Recipients must not speak on behalf of USDA or characterize USDA decision-making, policies, or future actions, including:

• Why projects were selected;

• How USDA evaluates proposals;

• Future funding rounds or budget decisions;

• USDA strategy, national priorities, or program direction;

• How your project fits into broader USDA policy decisions or the NWS response;

• Any inquiry that could be interpreted as a request for an official USDA position;

• Long-term operational planning, deployment strategy, regulatory implications, or national implementation; and,

• Predictions about future USDA actions or funding.

If media asks about any of the restricted items above, please direct them to screwworm@usda.gov . When redirecting, use phrasing such as: “I can speak to my team’s work on this project, but questions about USDA policy or future NWS response plans should be directed to the USDA.”

Press releases. Send draft press releases regarding your GC project for awareness to NWS.Grand.Challenge@usda.gov at least 5 business days in advance of posting. Include in the subject line of the email (1) APP ID # and FAIN agreement number and (2) “PR”.

Social media. If you would like to request USDA amplification, send social media posts to NWS.Grand.Challenge@usda.gov at least 5 business days in advance of posting. Include in the subject line of the email (1) APP ID # and FAIN agreement number and (2) “SOCIAL”.
